  {
   "say": "Where do we park Israel? You told me. We tried four spots.",
   "gap": 0.2
  },
  {
   "say": "Episode 3. Israel is out at sea, looking for a spot.",
   "screen": "Israel's Journey, *Episode 3*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Spot one: Russia's Jewish Autonomous Oblast. Stalin made it a Jewish homeland in 1934.",
   "screen": "*1934:* a Soviet Jewish homeland"
  },
  {
   "say": "Today, 837 Jews live there. January averages minus 21 degrees. The hummus freezes.",
   "screen": "*837* Jews. *-21°C* in January."
  },
  {
   "say": "Spot two: New York. Easy. 960,000 Jews already live in the city.",
   "screen": "New York City: *960,000* Jews"
  },
  {
   "say": "One problem. Israel is about the size of New Jersey. And New Jersey said: one is enough.",
   "screen": "Israel: about the size of *New Jersey*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Spot three: Indiana. Four Israels fit. Neighbours: Ohio and Kentucky. Biggest threat: corn.",
   "screen": "Indiana: *4* Israels fit"
  },
  {
   "say": "Spot four was Britain's idea, in 1903: land in East Africa.",
   "screen": "*1903:* Britain offers East Africa"
  },
  {
   "say": "In 1905, the Zionists said no, thanks.",
   "screen": "*1905:* no, thanks"
  },
  {
   "say": "Then one of you wrote: park it where it already is. It's perfect.",
   "screen": "Park it where it *already is*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Jews have lived there for three thousand years. So Israel sails home.",
   "screen": "*3,000* years. Back home."
  },
  {
   "say": "Millions of Palestinians call this land home too. Both peoples are here to stay.",
   "screen": "Both peoples are *here to stay*"
  },
  {
   "say": "Where would you park your country? Tell me below.",
   "screen": "Where would you park *your* country?"
  },
  {
   "follow": true
  },
  {
   "say": "Episode 4 is yours. So tell me:",
   "gap": 0.1
  }
 ],
